# Get Started with CompuTec MCP Server

In this guide, we'll show you how to enable CompuTec MCP Server for a test company, connect Claude Desktop, and ask Claude questions about your SAP Business One data.

## Before you start

Before you begin, make sure that:

- **CompuTec AppEngine 3.2509.1 or later** is installed and activated. [Read more](/docs/appengine/administrators-guide/configuration-and-administration/installation)
- **OIDC authentication** is enabled in **SAP Business One**. In the **Identity Providers** tab of the **SAP Business One System Landscape Directory (SLD)**, the **SAP Business One Authentication Server** is active.
- You have a test or demo company in **SAP Business One**, and it is active in **CompuTec AppEngine**.
- You have administrator access to the **CompuTec AppEngine Administration Panel**.
- You have **Claude Desktop** with a **Team** plan or **Claude for Work**, and necessary permissions, so that you can add a custom connector.

:::info[note]
Use a test or demo company. In this tutorial, you only read data. Don't use a production company until you have tested CompuTec MCP Server and checked the results.
:::

